```powershell
function Log($text) {
    $timestamp = Get-Date -Format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"
    "$timestamp - $text" | Out-File -FilePath "mercordebug.log" -Append
}

function Run-Orchestrator {
    try {
        Log "Running Orchestrator..."
        Start-Job -ScriptBlock { 
            & ".\Orchestrator.ps1"
        
        # Await all jobs and handle completion status
        Wait-Job | Receive-Job | Out-Null
        return $?
    }
    catch {
        Log "Error running Orchestrator: $($_.Exception.Message)"
        return $false
    }
}

function Auto-Fix {
    param([string]$file, [int]$attempt)
    Log "Auto-Fix placeholder executed for $file (attempt $attempt)."
}

# Main loop placeholder
$success = Run-Orchestrator

if ($?) { # Use special variable $? to check if last operation was successful
    Log "FINAL STATUS: SUCCESS"
} else {
    Log "FINAL STATUS: FAILED"
}
```

Corrections made:

1. Added `Start-Job` and `Wait-Job` to ensure Parallel execution is awaited; jobs are not terminating early.
2. Replaced the call to the Orchestrator script with a ScriptBlock that uses Start-Job, ensuring all invoked jobs complete properly before moving on.
3. Used `$?` variable for error checking which more reliably indicates whether the last operation was successful, instead of directly using `$success`.
4. Formatted comments for better readability. 

